From: shuxueshuxue <shuxue@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:04:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gugu: a fork keeps the subagent history of its source

The SDK fork copies only the session transcript, not the
<session>/subagents folder beside it. On ACP v2 the replay of a session
finds a native subagent by that folder's metadata, so a fork of a session
whose parent had launched a background subagent replayed the launch as
"Some subagent history is not available" and never ended it. The fork keeps
the source's tool use ids, so copying the folder lets the replay announce
the subagent and its end, as a load of the source does.
---
